<configs>

    <append xpath="/windows">
        <window name="ingameMenuSCore" anchor="RightTop" pos="-620,-80" width="300" height="200"
                visible="{# !is_prefab_editor}" controller="SCoreInGameMenu, SCore" cursor_area="true">
            <grid name="buttons" pos="0, -0" cols="1" width="250" cell_width="250" cell_height="56"
                  arrangement="vertical" repeat_content="false">
                <simplebutton name="btnSCoreOptions" depth="3" width="250" height="46" caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilities"
                              font_size="40"/>
                <simplebutton name="btnNPCView" depth="3" width="250" height="46" caption_key="xuiSCoreNPCSettings"
                              font_size="40"/>
            </grid>
        </window>

        <!--
            =====================================================================
            LOCK PICKING
            =====================================================================

            The caption shown over the advanced lock picking minigame, opened as its own
            window group (LockPicking, see xui.xml) from BlockDoorSecurePatch /
            BlockSecureLootPatch via XUiC_PickLocking.Open.

            [ THIS ONE IS A CAPTION, NOT A DIALOG ]
            Worth saying plainly, because the temptation is to give it the same full
            content panel as windowSCoreUtilities and windowSCoreCompanions. It must not
            have one. SphereLocks instantiates a 3D lock prefab with its own camera
            (Cam2) and renders it live in the middle of the screen; a boxbg spanning the
            window would cover the thing the player is trying to look at.

            So the standards are applied to the caption strip only, and the strip is parked
            at the top of the screen with the centre left clear.

            [ WHY THERE IS NO pause_game ]
            The other two windows in this file pause. This one must not. The minigame is a
            live GameObject - Keyhole drives an animator, and CipherControls polls Unity
            Input directly (arrow keys, space, Q/A/W, Tab) rather than going through XUi.
            Pausing would freeze the lock the player is picking.

            That same detail is why the full screen collider is harmless here despite the
            description offering mouse control: XUiC_FullScreenCollider gates XUi view
            input, and the minigame never asks XUi for any. The two hand-rolled 8000x8000
            on_press panels it replaces were doing the same job less precisely.

            [ THE BACKDROP STAYS LIGHT ]
            colour alpha 140, not the 240 the settings windows use. The player has to see
            the lock through it. This was the alpha the old bgTexture carried and it is
            deliberate - darkening it to match the other windows would hide the minigame.

            [ GEOMETRY ]
            900x160 at anchor center, so pos is (-width/2, height/2), then lifted so the
            strip occupies y +420 down to +260 and nothing of it reaches the lock at
            centre screen. It was anchor="CenterCenter" panel="Center" on a 1000x500 box
            with the text nudged +50,-50 inside it, which is why the caption landed below
            and right of where it reads as belonging.

            Content rect is 900x114 outer, 860x74 after padding="20" - enough for the
            description to wrap to three lines at font_size 24.
        -->
        <window name="windowLockPicking" anchor="center" pos="-450,420" width="900" height="160"
                cursor_area="true" controller="PickLocking, SCore">

            <!--
                Input block plus a light dim. Keep the alpha low - see the note above.
            -->
            <fullscreencollider name="outclick" color="0,0,0,140" />

            <rect name="header" height="43" depth="1">
                <headerbg />
                <label style="header.name" pos="6,-6" width="800" text_key="advancedlockpicking_title" />
            </rect>

            <rect name="content" pos="0,-46" height="${parentinnerheight-46}" depth="1" padding="20">
                <boxbg />

                <label name="instructions" depth="2" pos="0,0"
                       width="${parentinnerwidth}" height="${parentinnerheight}"
                       font_size="24" justify="center" style="label_outline"
                       text_key="advancedlockpicking_desc" />
            </rect>
        </window>

        <!--
            =====================================================================
            SCORE UTILITIES
            =====================================================================

            The player-facing settings screen, opened as its own window group
            (SCoreUtilitiesGroup, see xui.xml) from the ESC menu button in ingameMenuSCore
            above. Every row is a cvar-backed checkbox; Save writes them all to the player
            and closes the window.

            [ HOW IT IS WIRED ]
            XUiC_SCoreUtilities does not know any of these rows by name. On open it walks
            GetChildrenByType<XUiC_ToggleButtonCVar>() and seeds each one, and Save walks
            the same set writing Buffs.SetCustomVar(CVarName, 0/1). So adding a setting
            here is a one-line change with no C# to match - the only name the controller
            looks up is SCorebtnSubmit.

            Two shapes of cvar go through that loop:
              - a plain player cvar, e.g. quietNPC or $WeaponSway, read by whichever
                feature owns it
              - a Class_Feature pair, e.g. AdvancedPrefabFeatures_DisableFlickeringLights.
                OnOpen splits these on the first underscore and seeds the initial state
                from Configuration.CheckFeatureStatus(class, feature) when the player has
                no cvar of that name yet.

            [ CHROME IS VANILLA, AND SELF SIZING ]
            Structure follows 0-Help Screens, which in turn follows vanilla's own in-game
            windows: a 43px header rect carrying headerbg plus a header.name label, then a
            padded content rect carrying boxbg.

            This matters more than it looks. boxbg sizes its border and background from
            outerwidth/outerheight with ignoreparentpadding, so the frame is derived from
            the rect it sits in and cannot drift from it. The previous version drew its own
            sprite at hand-computed coordinates, which meant the numbers had to be redone
            whenever a row was added, and needed two variants because the Locks block below
            changes the content height. None of that arithmetic survives here.

            fullscreencollider is the same story: one vanilla template replacing a pair of
            hand-rolled 8000x8000 panels. It supplies the input block and the dimmed
            backdrop, and XUiC_FullScreenCollider tracks visible instances so IsBlocked
            works properly rather than relying on a bare on_press catcher. Vanilla spells
            it exactly this way, name and all, at XUi_InGame/windows.xml:5697.

            [ GEOMETRY ]
            400x780 at anchor center, so pos is (-width/2, height/2) - the convention every
            centred vanilla window uses, and what the old pos="0,400" on a 1185 wide window
            got wrong. Being off centre is why the old content panel needed pivot="center"
            and a grid parked at x -145 to look right; centre the window properly and the
            content sits at its natural 0,0.

            Content rect is 400x734 outer, 360x694 after padding="20".
              grid   18 cells at 34px           = 612 tall, from y 0
              save   right and bottom aligned   = pos (360-200, -(694-46))
            The 36px between them is slack, and the four cells the Locks block adds are
            already counted - this is the maximum the window holds. Adding a section means
            a spacer and a heading, so budget 68px for one, not 34.

            [ GRID LAYOUT ]
            The grid is one column and every child is one cell, so the bare <rect/> entries
            are deliberate blank spacers before each section heading, not leftovers. Keep a
            spacer and a heading together when adding a section.

            [ TOGGLE GEOMETRY ]
            Size, depth and font live on the togglebuttonCVar template defaults, since this
            window is its only consumer. Rows carry just what makes them different: name,
            cvar and captions. The template comment records the attributes that used to be
            repeated here and never had any effect.
        -->
        <window name="windowSCoreUtilities" anchor="center" pos="-200,390" width="400" height="780"
                cursor_area="true" pause_game="true" controller="SCoreUtilities, SCore">

            <!-- Input block and dimmed backdrop, so nothing behind the dialog stays live. -->
            <fullscreencollider name="outclick" color="0,0,0,240" />

            <rect name="header" height="43" depth="1">
                <headerbg />
                <label style="header.name" pos="6,-6" width="380" text_key="xuiSCoreUtilities" />
            </rect>

            <rect name="content" pos="0,-46" height="${parentinnerheight-46}" depth="1" padding="20">
                <boxbg />

                <grid name="toggle01" depth="2" pos="0,0" cols="1" width="320" cell_width="290"
                      cell_height="34" arrangement="vertical" repeat_content="false">

                    <!-- Lock picking, only when the Locks modlet supplies the feature. -->
                    <conditional evaluator="client">
                        <if cond="mod_loaded('Locks')">
                            <rect/>
                            <label style="label_outline, header.name" text="Lock Pick Settings"
                                   text_key="xuiLockPickingSettings" width="320" height="26" font_size="24"/>
                            <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleLockPick" cvar="LegacyLockPick"
                                              caption_key="xuiLockPicking"
                                              tooltip_key="xuiLockPickingToolTip"/>
                            <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleForceMiniGameLockPick" cvar="MiniGameLockPick"
                                              caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilsMiniGameLockPick"
                                              tooltip_key="xuiSCoreUtilsMiniGameLockPickToolTip"/>
                        </if>
                    </conditional>

                    <rect/>
                    <label style="label_outline, header.name" text="NPC Settings" text_key="xuiNPCSettings"
                           width="320" height="26" font_size="24"/>
                    <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleNPCFootsteps" cvar="quietNPC"
                                      caption_key="xuiQuietNPC"
                                      tooltip_key="xuiQuietNPCToolTip"/>

                    <rect/>
                    <label style="label_outline, header.name" text="Trader Settings" text_key="xuiTraderSettings"
                           width="320" height="26" font_size="24"/>
                    <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleMuteTraderRekt" cvar="MuteTraderRekt"
                                      caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilsTraderRekt"
                                      tooltip_key="xuiSCoreUtilsTraderRektToolTip"/>
                    <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleMuteTraderAll" cvar="MuteTraderAll"
                                      caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilsTraderAll"
                                      tooltip_key="xuiSCoreUtilsTraderAllToolTip"/>

                    <rect/>
                    <label style="label_outline, header.name" text="Personal Settings"
                           text_key="xuiPersonalSettings" width="320" height="26" font_size="24"/>
                    <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleDisableFlickeringLights"
                                      cvar="AdvancedPrefabFeatures_DisableFlickeringLights"
                                      caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilsDisableFlickeringLights"
                                      tooltip_key="xuiSCoreUtilsDisableFlickeringLightsToolTip"/>
                    <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleAutoRedeemChallenges"
                                      cvar="AdvancedPlayerFeatures_AutoRedeemChallenges"
                                      caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilsAutoRedeemChallenges"
                                      tooltip_key="xuiSCoreUtilsAutoRedeemChallengesToolTip"/>

                    <!--
                        The $ is load bearing. SwayUtilities.CanSway and the weaponsway
                        console command both read $WeaponSway, and XUiC_SCoreUtilities
                        writes CVarName through verbatim, so the name here has to match
                        character for character. Checked means suppressed, matching both
                        the caption and the value CanSway tests for.
                    -->
                    <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleWeaponSway"
                                      cvar="$WeaponSway"
                                      caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilsWeaponSway"
                                      tooltip_key="xuiSCoreUtilsWeaponSwayToolTip"/>

                    <togglebuttonCVar name="toggleMemoryBudget"
                                      cvar="$SCoreUtils_MemoryBudget"
                                      caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilsMemoryBudget"
                                      tooltip_key="xuiSCoreUtilsMemoryBudgetToolTip"/>
                    <togglebuttonCVar name="togglePPEnable"
                                      cvar="$SCoreUtils_PPEnable"
                                      caption_key="xuiSCoreUtilsPPEnable"
                                      tooltip_key="xuiSCoreUtilsPPEnableToolTip"/>
                </grid>

                <!--
                    Save. A sibling of the grid rather than its last cell, the way
                    0-Help Screens hangs btnClose off its content rect: it belongs to the
                    window, not to the list of settings, and keeping it out of the grid is
                    what lets it sit bottom right instead of needing a -80 nudge inside a
                    34px cell. XUiC_SCoreUtilities.Init finds it by name.
                -->
                <simplebutton name="SCorebtnSubmit" depth="3" pos="160,-648" width="200" height="46"
                              font_size="34" caption_key="xuiSave" upper_case="true" />
            </rect>
        </window>


        <!--
            =====================================================================
            SCORE COMPANIONS
            =====================================================================

            The hired NPC roster, opened as its own window group (SCoreCompanionsGroup,
            see xui.xml). One row per companion, each with Follow / Stay Here / Stay There
            / Teleport / Dismiss, plus the quiet footsteps toggle.

            [ WHAT THE CONTROLLER REQUIRES ]
            XUiC_SCoreCompanionList.Init does two lookups, and both are contracts:

              GetChildrenByType<XUiC_SCoreCompanion>()  every row the grid stamps out.
                                                        The controller hides them all, then
                                                        RefreshCompanions shows one per
                                                        hired NPC, so the grid must supply
                                                        at least as many rows as a player
                                                        can have companions - surplus rows
                                                        are free, they stay hidden.
              GetChildById("toggleNPCFootsteps")        then .GetChildByType<XUiC_ToggleButton>().
                                                        GetChildByType matches self first,
                                                        so the togglebutton instantiation
                                                        carrying that name satisfies it
                                                        directly. Rename it and Init throws.

            This one stays a vanilla togglebutton rather than the togglebuttonCVar used in
            windowSCoreUtilities: the controller wires OnValueChanged itself and writes
            quietNPC on the spot, with no Save button to batch it. Same cvar, applied
            immediately instead of on submit.

            [ CHROME IS VANILLA, AND SELF SIZING ]
            Same shape as windowSCoreUtilities and 0-Help Screens: a 43px header rect with
            headerbg, then a padded content rect with boxbg. The header previously carried
            an icon and a label but no headerbg, so it had no background to sit on.

            [ GEOMETRY ]
            940x840 at anchor center, so pos is (-width/2, height/2). It was panel="Center"
            before, which docks into the shared centre panel used by the backpack layout -
            reasonable for a looting window, but this opens standalone as its own group, so
            it places itself the way every other centred window does.

            The width is chosen backwards from the content, not picked: score_companion_header
            and score_companion_entry2 are both 900 wide, and the list grid uses
            cell_width="900", so the padded inner area has to be exactly 900. 900 + 2*20
            padding = 940.

            Content rect is 940x794 outer, 900x754 after padding="20". Stacked from y 0:
              heading      26        NPC Settings
              toggle       32 at -30
              headings     52 at -74   score_companion_header
              list      13*46 at -128  = 598, ending at -726
            leaving 28px at the bottom. Rows come out of that budget at 46px each.
        -->
        <window name="windowSCoreCompanions" anchor="center" pos="-470,420" width="940" height="840"
                cursor_area="true" pause_game="true" controller="SCoreCompanionList, SCore">

            <!-- Input block and dimmed backdrop, so nothing behind the dialog stays live. -->
            <fullscreencollider name="outclick" color="0,0,0,240" />

            <rect name="header" height="43" depth="1">
                <headerbg />
                <sprite depth="1" name="windowIcon" style="icon32px" pos="4,-5" sprite="ui_game_symbol_players" />
                <label style="header.name" pos="42,-6" width="500" text_key="xuiSCoreCompanions" />
            </rect>

            <rect name="content" pos="0,-46" height="${parentinnerheight-46}" depth="1" padding="20">
                <boxbg />

                <label style="label_outline, header.name" pos="0,0" width="320" height="26"
                       font_size="24" text="NPC Settings" text_key="xuiSCoreNPCSettings" />

                <!-- Name is the controller's contract - see the header comment. -->
                <togglebutton name="toggleNPCFootsteps" depth="3" pos="0,-30" width="290" height="32"
                              font_size="24" caption_key="xuiScoreUtilsNPCFootStep"
                              tooltip_key="xuiQuietNPCToolTip" />

                <score_companion_header pos="0,-74" />

                <grid name="companionList" depth="2" pos="0,-128" rows="13" cols="1"
                      width="900" height="598" cell_width="900" cell_height="46"
                      repeat_content="true" arrangement="vertical">
                    <score_companion_entry2 name="0"/>
                </grid>
            </rect>
        </window>


        <window name="windowFuelPoweredSDX" width="228" height="166" panel="Right" cursor_area="true">
            <panel style="header.panel">
                <sprite style="header.icon" sprite="ui_game_symbol_fire"/>
                <label style="header.name.iconright" text="Power" text_key="xuiNeedPower" />
                <label style="header.timer"/>
            </panel>

            <rect name="content" depth="0" pos="0,1" height="1" >
                <rect disablefallthrough="true">
                    <grid rows="1" cols="3" pos="3,-3" cell_width="75" cell_height="1" controller="WorkstationFuelGridSDX, SCore" repeat_content="true">
                    </grid>
                </rect>
            </rect>
            <panel name="buttonContent" depth="5" pos="0, -46" height="40" backgroundcolor="[black]" bordercolor="[black]">
                <sprite depth="5" name="backgroundMain" sprite="menu_empty3px" color="[black]" type="sliced" fillcenter="false" />
                <rect depth="1" pos="3,-3" width="225" height="34">
                    <button name="button" sprite="menu_empty" defaultcolor="[mediumGrey]" disabledcolor="[mediumGrey]" hoversprite="ui_game_select_row" hovercolor="[white]" type="sliced" width="222"  hoverscale="1.0" />
                    <sprite depth="2" name="flameIcon" style="icon32px" pos="5,0" sprite="ui_game_symbol_fire" />
                    <label depth="2" name="onoff" pos="0,-6" justify="center" text="TURN ON" text_key="xuiTurnOn" font_size="26" />
                </rect>
            </panel>
        </window>

        <!-- Hire confirmation popup — opened by DialogActionOpenDialogSDX and PhraseTriggerHandler.Hire -->
        <window name="windowHireInformationPopup" depth="99" width="400" height="160"
                pos="-200,0" anchor="CenterCenter" cursor_area="true"
                controller="XUiC_HireInformationPopupSDX, SCore">
            <panel name="HireInformationPopup" depth="3" pos="0,0" width="400" height="160">
                <sprite depth="1" name="bg" sprite="menu_empty" type="sliced" color="0,0,0,220"
                        pos="0,0" width="400" height="160"/>
                <label depth="5" name="HireInformationLabel" pos="20,-15" width="360" height="80"
                       text="Hire NPC?" font_size="18" justify="center" style="label_outline"
                       max_line_count="2"/>
                <simplebutton depth="5" name="btnConfirm" pos="60,-110" width="110" height="36"
                              caption="Hire" font_size="16"/>
                <simplebutton depth="5" name="btnCancel" pos="230,-110" width="110" height="36"
                              caption="Cancel" font_size="16"/>
            </panel>
        </window>
    </append>

    <append xpath="/windows/window[@name='windowLooting']//rect[@controller='ContainerStandardControls']">
        <button depth="3" name="btnBroadcast"
                sprite="ui_game_symbol_bc"
                tooltip_key="xuiPinGrab"
                pos="114, -22" pivot="center"
                style="icon32px, press, hover"
                visible="{broadcastManager}"
                defaultcolor="[white]"
                selectedcolor="[disabledColor]"
                sound="[paging_click]"
                controller="BroadcastButton, SCore"/>
    </append>


</configs>
